INT. FUNICULAR STATION - HOLDING ROOM - NIGHT

A tiled waiting room at the top of a cable railway, converted overnight into a police holding space. A bench, a radiator, a vending machine with an out-of-order sign. Cable machinery groans through the wall.

INSPECTOR MALCOLM TREVENNA, 50s, sits on the bench with a thermos. Across from him, a handcuffed prisoner, DESIREE LACROIX-ODUYA, 30s, sits upright and calm, her coat folded in her lap. A uniformed sergeant, SERGEANT BRANWELL KUTTNER, 40s, leans on the doorframe, arms folded.

TREVENNA
You can drop the act now.

DESIREE
Which act is that?

TREVENNA
The one where you don't know why you're here.

DESIREE
I know exactly why I'm here.

TREVENNA
Then say it.

DESIREE
You saw a woman leave a building with a bag.

TREVENNA
A bag containing sixty thousand pounds.

DESIREE
A bag containing sixty thousand pounds of someone else's money. I carried it. I did not take it.

TREVENNA
Distinction without difference.

DESIREE
Then arrest the bag.

KUTTNER
Inspector, she's baiting you.

TREVENNA
I'm aware, Sergeant.

DESIREE
Is the funicular running?

TREVENNA
It's midnight.

DESIREE
So there's no way down.

TREVENNA
There's the road.

DESIREE
Which you closed.

TREVENNA
Which we closed.

DESIREE
You don't have a car.

TREVENNA
We have a Sergeant.

DESIREE
Who has a car?

KUTTNER
Who has a bicycle.

DESIREE
I see.

A door opens with a gust of cold air. VIOLETA SANDOVAL-GRAY, 60s, a silver-haired woman in a camel coat, enters carrying a briefcase. She sets it on the bench and unclasps it with a flourish.

VIOLETA
Good evening, gentlemen. I'm Ms. Lacroix-Oduya's solicitor. Release her.

TREVENNA
On what grounds?

VIOLETA
On the grounds that I have the receipt.

TREVENNA
What receipt?

VIOLETA
For the sixty thousand pounds. From a registered charity. Signed this afternoon.

TREVENNA
That's a forgery.

VIOLETA
It is notarized.

TREVENNA
By whom?

VIOLETA
By me.

DESIREE
(softly)
Oh, Violeta.

VIOLETA
Hush, dear.

TREVENNA
This is absurd.

VIOLETA
Inspector, would you rather be absurd or wrong?

KUTTNER
(low)
Sir, she has a point.

TREVENNA
Sergeant, which side are you on?

KUTTNER
The side with the bicycle.

A long silence. Trevenna looks at the receipt, at the briefcase, at the radiator. He sighs. He unlocks the cuffs.

TREVENNA
Take her. Go.

DESIREE
Thank you, Inspector.

TREVENNA
Don't thank me. Take the road.

VIOLETA
We will.

DESIREE
Goodnight, Sergeant.

KUTTNER
Mind the ice.
